    "title": "Utah Jazz TV Schedule",
    "text": "See how to watch or stream Utah Jazz games throughout the 2025-26 NBA season with the following TV schedule. (Full NBA schedule available here.) This site may earn a commission on subscriptions purchased via this page. Today Time (UTC)Game / TV1:00 amDenver Nuggets vs Utah JazzNBA League Pass | A ALT2, KTVD | H KJZZ Friday, April 3 Time (UTC)Game / TV12:00 amUtah Jazz vs Houston RocketsNBA League Pass | A KJZZ | H SCHN Sunday, April 5 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:00 pmUtah Jazz vs Oklahoma City ThunderNBA League Pass | A KJZZ | H FDSN OK | SN Tuesday, April 7 Time (UTC)Game / TV12:00 amUtah Jazz vs New Orleans PelicansNBA League Pass | A KJZZ | H GCSEN Friday, April 10 Time (UTC)Game / TV1:30 amMemphis Grizzlies vs Utah JazzNBA League Pass | A FDSN SE-MEM | H KJZZ Sunday, April 12 Time (UTC)Game / TV12:30 amUtah Jazz vs Los Angeles LakersNBA League Pass | A KJZZ | H SPECSN | NBA TV Canada No more upcoming games to show. How to Watch the Utah Jazz The Utah Jazz continue their prolonged rebuild behind returning star Lauri Markkanen and #5 draft pick Ace Bailey. Utah is unsurprisingly set for just four national TV games this season, two on NBC Sports and two on NBA TV. One of the NBC games is a January 27 matchup with the Clippers that will air on NBC affiliates in the Mountain and Pacific time zones, while the other — a February 23 matchup with Houston — is exclusive to Peacock. Locally, 78 Jazz games are scheduled to air on independent Salt Lake City affiliate KJZZ. Those games will also be available to watch on the Jazz+ direct-to-subscriber streaming service. Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (Jazz+): Jazz+ (in-market only): Jazz games can be streamed through the Jazz+ app for $20/mo or $126/year. For $175/year, subscribers can bundle the Jazz and NHL Mammoth through SEG+. NBA League Pass (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games, plus NBA TV. Also available as a standalone purchase through Amazon Prime Video. National games (ESPN/ABC, NBC/Peacock and Prime Video): Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Amazon Prime Video: All Amazon-produced games on Prime Video, plus the ability to purchase NBA League Pass and FanDuel Sports Network as add-ons. Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $100 off YouTube TV ($20 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3); NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network; NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC, the NBC broadcast network and KJZZ. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. In-Person See the Jazz in person at the Delta Center, or catch them on the road, by purchasing tickets from Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
